 and kidney pies. Hot water crust is traditionally used for producing hand-made pies."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-hot-water-crust-pastry"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_water_crust_pastry"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["English cuisine","cuisine/english-cuisine",[["Pork pie","dish/pork-pie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Pork jelly","ingredient/pork-jelly"]]}]},"dish/taqueria-el-califa-de-leon":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/taqueria-el-califa-de-leon","n":"Taquería El Califa de León","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Taquería El Califa de León is a taqueria in Colonia San Rafael, Cuauhtémoc, Mexico City. It was founded in 1968 by Juan Hernández González. Its menu is limited to a small variety of beef tacos made with hand-made tortillas. The restaurant received a Michelin star in 2024, the first Mexican taco stand so awarded. The taquería lost its only Michelin star in May 2026."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-taqueria-el-califa-de-leon"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taquer%C3%ADa_El_Califa_de_Le%C3%B3n"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Pati Jinich","ref":"site/patijinich-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Acapulco Mexican Restaurant and Cantin